# Overtime — a night shift at the pizzeria, from the other side of the desk.
# Non-explicit. Written for the Aside engine.
#
# Themes: being kept for a purpose you didn't pick; performing an identity
# for an audience that has gone home; what is left of a person when the
# audience stops watching. The cast are people, not threats. The threat is
# the job, and the fact that nobody in this building is allowed to leave it.

title: Overtime
author: Roxanne
start: n1_start

# ============================================================
# NIGHT ONE — the chair, the hall, the curtain
# ============================================================

== n1_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
The office has two doors, one fan, and no window.
The fan is the only thing in the building that does not want anything from you.
You have a name badge. The name on it is yours. The photograph is not.
-> n1_monty

== n1_monty ==
sfx door_open
show monty neutral at left
monty: New one.
monty: You are in her chair.

* "Who was she?" -> n1_whowas
* "I will move, if you want it." -> n1_move
* Say nothing. -> n1_silence

== n1_whowas ==
~ aff_monty -1
monty: Does not matter.
monty (flat): She is gone and you are here. That is the whole story.
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_move ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: It is a chair.
monty (tired): She would have laughed at you for saying that.
~ asked_about_her true
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_silence ==
~ aff_monty +2
~ let_quiet_stand true
monty: ...
monty: Huh.
monty (quiet): Most of them fill the quiet. You did not.
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_hall ==
bg west_hall
music none
The west hall runs long and dark and smells faintly of birthday cake.
Somewhere behind you the fan keeps turning, and keeps not caring.
sfx footstep
roxanne: I heard the door.
show roxanne smirk at center
roxanne: You are not supposed to be back here.

* "Neither are you." -> n1_banter
* "I am doing my rounds." -> n1_rounds
* "I know. I will go." -> n1_retreat

== n1_banter ==
~ aff_roxy +2
roxanne (laughs): No. I am not.
roxanne: But I have been here longer, so I win.
show roxanne warm at center
roxanne (warm): ...You are not scared of me.
roxanne: That is either brave or stupid and I have not decided which.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove

== n1_rounds ==
~ aff_roxy +1
roxanne: Rounds. Sure.
roxanne (flat): You know what I do on my rounds? I check that you are still breathing.
roxanne: Nobody asks me to. There is just nothing else to do at three in the morning.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove

== n1_retreat ==
~ aff_roxy -1
roxanne: Good.
roxanne (cold): Keep walking.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove_cold

== n1_cove ==
bg cove
music music_box
The curtain is drawn, and something behind it is being very still.
You get the feeling it has been practising.
freddy: Hm.
show freddy idle at right
freddy: You can hear me. That is further than most get.

* "I can hear you." -> n1_hear
* "Who are you?" -> n1_name
* "What is this place?" -> n1_place

== n1_hear ==
~ aff_freddy +2
~ listened +1
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): Then stay a minute.
freddy: That is all anybody has ever wanted, you know. A minute, and someone actually listening.
-> n1_offer

== n1_name ==
freddy: A longer answer than you have time for.
freddy (wry): Ask me again once you have done a week. You will have earned it.
-> n1_offer

== n1_place ==
~ listened +1
freddy: A restaurant that closes at nine.
freddy: And then stays open. For us. Only for us.
freddy (wry): Nobody has ever explained what we are supposed to be doing in here.
-> n1_offer

== n1_offer ==
freddy: There is a song that plays when the power dies.
freddy: I do not choose it. I am just the one standing there when it stops.
freddy: Chica is in the kitchen. She would like you, probably.
freddy: She likes everyone. It is the only thing left that she is allowed to do.
hide freddy
-> n1_kitchen

== n1_kitchen ==
bg east_corner
music none
The east corner is colder than the rest of the building.
sfx pot_clank
chica: Oh!
show chica neutral at center
chica: You are the new one. Hello. Hi.
chica (bright): I am Chica, I do the kitchen, I have done the kitchen for a long time.

* "It is nice to meet you, Chica." -> n1_chica_nice
* "Why are you still working?" -> n1_chica_why
* Just watch her. -> n1_chica_watch

== n1_chica_nice ==
~ aff_chica +2
chica: ...
chica (bright): Nice to meet me. Nice to meet me.
chica: I will be thinking about that for hours now. That is not a complaint.
~ asked_about_her true
-> n1_end

== n1_chica_why ==
~ aff_chica +1
chica: Because the kitchen does not finish.
chica: I clean it, and then it is dirty again, and then I clean it.
chica (flat): It is the only way I know it is still night.
-> n1_end

== n1_chica_watch ==
~ aff_chica -1
~ let_quiet_stand true
chica: ...
chica (small): You are going to be one of the quiet ones.
chica: That is alright. I am good at those.
-> n1_end

== n1_cove_cold ==
bg cove
The curtain stays shut. You do not knock, and it does not open.
You get the sense that this was a test, and that you failed it politely.
-> n1_end

== n1_end ==
bg office_night
music none
The lights come up at six like nothing happened at all.
Everything in the building is exactly where it was.
-> n1_dawn_check

== n1_dawn_check ==
if listened >= 1 and aff_chica >= 2 -> n1_dawn_good
if aff_monty >= 2 or aff_roxy >= 2 -> n1_dawn_mixed
-> n1_dawn_flat

== n1_dawn_good ==
You learned a name and used it, which is more than the badge ever did.
The badge says you are employed here. After tonight that is not quite the same word it was.
~ nights +1
-> n2_start

== n1_dawn_mixed ==
You got a laugh out of one of them and a silence out of another.
It is a start. It is the kind of start that costs somebody something.
~ nights +1
-> n2_start

== n1_dawn_flat ==
You did your rounds. You checked the doors. You left at six.
Nothing in this building will remember that you were here, and that is the job.
-> n2_start

# ============================================================
# NIGHT TWO — names, and what a party looks like a week later
# ============================================================

== n2_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
Second night. The fan is already running, which means someone turned it on for you.
That is either a courtesy or a habit, and you cannot tell which.
-> n2_monty

== n2_monty ==
bg dining
music none
show monty neutral at left
The dining room is laid out for a party. Paper hats, paper cups, a tablecloth with a stain
shaped like a hand. Somebody set this up and nobody ever took it down.
monty: You came back.

* "I said I would." -> n2_came_back
* "I work here." -> n2_work
* "I wanted to." -> n2_wanted [if aff_monty >= 2]

== n2_came_back ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: People say that.
monty (tired): They say it on the way out, mostly.
-> n2_tables

== n2_work ==
~ aff_monty -1
monty: Right.
monty (flat): Work.
-> n2_tables

== n2_wanted ==
~ aff_monty +2
monty: ...
monty (quiet): That is a different sentence.
monty: I do not know what to do with that one.
-> n2_tables

== n2_tables ==
monty: This is what it looks like a week after a party.
monty: Nobody clears it. They just turn the lights off and it is our room instead of theirs.
monty (flat): I have eaten nothing. I have been at that table for eleven years.

* "What were you before this?" -> n2_before
* "Eleven years." -> n2_eleven
* "Do you want it cleared?" -> n2_cleared

== n2_before ==
~ asked_about_her true
monty: Before this I was not.
monty: That is the honest answer and you will not like it much.
-> n2_freddy

== n2_eleven ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: Eleven years. Give or take the nights nobody came.
monty: I stopped counting because the counting was the only thing that moved.
-> n2_freddy

== n2_cleared ==
~ aff_monty +2
monty: ...
monty (quiet): Nobody has ever asked me that.
monty: No. I do not want it cleared. It is the last thing they left that says somebody was here.
-> n2_freddy

== n2_freddy ==
bg cove_open
music music_box
hide monty
The curtain is open. Freddy is standing in front of it rather than behind it,
which feels like being let into a room.
show freddy idle at right
freddy: You are back. That is twice now.

* "Does that matter?" -> n2_matter
* "Is that unusual?" -> n2_unusual

== n2_matter ==
freddy: It does to me.
freddy (warm): I keep a very small ledger, you know. There is not much in it.
-> n2_ledger

== n2_unusual ==
~ aff_freddy +1
freddy: Yes.
freddy (wry): People usually have the decency to leave eventually.
freddy: The last one did not leave. That was worse.
-> n2_ledger

== n2_ledger ==
freddy: I have been trying to work out what we are for.
freddy: Not what we do. We know what we do. We sing, we wave, we serve.
freddy (wry): I mean the afterwards. The part nobody wrote down.

* "Do you think there is an afterwards?" -> n2_afterwards
* "Maybe there is not one." -> n2_none

== n2_afterwards ==
~ listened +1
freddy: Something plays a song when the power goes. I do not know who chose it.
freddy: That is as close as I have got to an answer.
-> n2_roxanne

== n2_none ==
~ aff_freddy -1
freddy: Then I have been doing a great deal of thinking about nothing.
freddy (idle): I would rather you were wrong.
-> n2_roxanne

== n2_roxanne ==
bg west_hall
music none
hide freddy
sfx footstep
show roxanne smirk at center
roxanne: He does that to everyone. The ledger speech.
roxanne: I used to think it was for me. It is for whoever is in the room.

* "Was it for her?" -> n2_her
* "Are you jealous?" -> n2_jealous
* Say nothing. -> n2_her_quiet

== n2_her ==
~ aff_roxy +1
roxanne: It was for her, yes.
roxanne (flat): She got the whole speech. Twice. Then she stopped coming.
-> n2_who

== n2_jealous ==
~ aff_roxy +2
roxanne: ...
roxanne (laughs): God. Yes. Obviously yes.
show roxanne warm at center
roxanne (warm): You are the first one who has asked me a real question.
-> n2_who

== n2_her_quiet ==
~ aff_roxy +1
~ let_quiet_stand true
roxanne: You do the quiet thing too.
roxanne (flat): He likes it. I have never worked out what to do with it.
-> n2_who

== n2_who ==
The hall light over the door has a name written on it in marker.
It has been washed over so many times that the letters are only a bruise now.
roxanne: She was on the door. Then she was not.

* "What was her name?" -> n2_name
* "What happened to her?" -> n2_happened
* "This is not my business." -> n2_business

== n2_name ==
~ aff_roxy +2
~ knows_her_name true
roxanne: Nia.
roxanne (warm): There. Now you know something about her and I am not the only one holding it.
~ listened +1
-> n2_chica

== n2_happened ==
~ aff_roxy +1
roxanne: She finished a shift and did not come back.
roxanne (flat): That is all. There is no story. There is just a door with her name on it.
-> n2_chica

== n2_business ==
~ aff_roxy -2
roxanne: Oh.
roxanne (cold): Right. No. It is not.
hide roxanne
-> n2_chica_noshow

== n2_chica ==
hide roxanne
bg east_corner
music none
-> n2_chica_body

== n2_chica_noshow ==
bg east_corner
music none
-> n2_chica_body

== n2_chica_body ==
show chica neutral at center
chica: Hello again.
chica (bright): I made you something. It is not a cake. I want to be clear that it is not a cake.

* "What is it?" -> n2_what
* "Thank you." -> n2_thanks
* Don't take it. -> n2_decline

== n2_what ==
chica: It is the shape of a cake.
chica (small): I cannot make the inside of it. I have never been able to.
-> n2_end

== n2_thanks ==
~ aff_chica +2
chica: ...
chica (bright): You said thank you. To me. For the shape of a cake.
chica: I am going to have a very good shift now.
-> n2_end

== n2_decline ==
~ aff_chica -2
chica: Oh. That is fine.
chica (small): I knew it was not right. I knew before I brought it.
-> n2_end

== n2_end ==
bg office_night
music none
Six o'clock. The lights do the same calm thing they did yesterday.
-> n2_dawn

== n2_dawn ==
if knows_her_name and aff_roxy >= 3 -> n2_dawn_name
if listened >= 2 -> n2_dawn_partial
-> n2_dawn_plain

== n2_dawn_name ==
You leave carrying a name you were not given officially.
It is the first thing anybody in this building has trusted you with.
~ nights +1
-> n3_start

== n2_dawn_partial ==
Something is being built here, slowly, out of small sentences.
You are not sure yet who it is for.
~ nights +1
-> n3_start

== n2_dawn_plain ==
You did the rounds. You checked the doors. You learned nothing you could write down.
-> n3_start

# ============================================================
# NIGHT THREE - the notice
# ============================================================

== n3_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
There is a piece of paper on the wall that was not there yesterday.
It is taped at all four corners, which is how you can tell it is not a joke.
-> n3_notice

== n3_notice ==
It says TEMPORARY CLOSURE PENDING ASSESSMENT, in the flat font that
companies use when they want a sentence to have no author.
Below it, smaller: thank you for your understanding.
You read it four times. It does not change.
-> n3_monty

== n3_monty ==
bg dining
music none
show monty neutral at left
monty: You have seen it.
monty (flat): Do not tell me what it says. I can read. I have had eleven years of practice.

* "How long have you known?" -> n3_known
* "It might not mean anything." -> n3_nothing
* Say nothing. -> n3_quiet

== n3_known ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: Since the woman came with the clipboard.
monty: She counted the tables. She did not count us.
monty (tired): That is the part I keep coming back to.
-> n3_freddy

== n3_nothing ==
~ aff_monty -1
monty: It means something.
monty (flat): Everything here means something. That is the whole problem with this building.
-> n3_freddy

== n3_quiet ==
~ aff_monty +2
~ let_quiet_stand true
monty: ...
monty (quiet): You are doing the quiet thing again.
monty: It works on me. I want you to know that it works.
-> n3_freddy

== n3_freddy ==
bg cove_open
music music_box
hide monty
show freddy idle at right
freddy: They count us now. Did you know that.
freddy: For eleven years nobody counted us. Now there is a number and the number is a list
and the list has a line through some of it.

* "Do you know which line?" -> n3_which
* "Maybe it will be fine." -> n3_fine

== n3_which ==
~ aff_freddy +1
freddy: No.
freddy (wry): I asked. She wrote something down and left, which I am told is an answer.
-> n3_chica

== n3_fine ==
~ aff_freddy -1
freddy: You are the fourth person to tell me that.
freddy (idle): The other three were staff, and they were all gone by the next week.
-> n3_chica

== n3_chica ==
bg east_corner
music none
hide freddy
sfx pot_clank
show chica neutral at center
chica: I have been cleaning all night.
chica (bright): Everything is very clean. You can check. It is the cleanest it has ever been.

* "Chica. The notice." -> n3_chica_notice
* "It is very clean." -> n3_chica_agree

== n3_chica_notice ==
~ aff_chica +1
chica: ...
chica (small): If it is clean they might keep it.
chica: That is not how it works, is it.
-> n3_roxanne

== n3_chica_agree ==
~ aff_chica +2
chica (bright): Thank you.
chica: If someone says it is clean, then it is clean. That is how I know things.
chica (small): I would like somebody to say it about me.
-> n3_roxanne

== n3_roxanne ==
bg west_hall
music none
hide chica
sfx footstep
show roxanne flat at center
roxanne: Do not.
roxanne (cold): Whatever you are about to say to her, do not.

* "What do I say instead?" -> n3_instead
* "She deserves the truth." -> n3_truth
* "You are frightened too." -> n3_frightened [if aff_roxy >= 3]

== n3_instead ==
~ aff_roxy +2
roxanne: Nothing. You say nothing to her.
roxanne (flat): I have been saying nothing to her for eleven years. I am extremely good at it.
-> n3_choice

== n3_truth ==
~ aff_roxy -1
roxanne: She deserves it.
roxanne (cold): And? I have watched what the truth does to her. It is not a kindness. It is a hobby.
-> n3_choice

== n3_frightened ==
~ aff_roxy +3
~ knows_roxanne true
roxanne: ...
show roxanne warm at center
roxanne (warm): Yes.
roxanne: I am the one who performs. That is the job. If I stop performing there is no Roxanne,
there is just a very loud machine that is frightened of a piece of paper.
-> n3_choice

== n3_choice ==
bg office_night
music none
hide roxanne
You are back in the office. The notice is still on the wall. It will be there at six.
You have about forty minutes and three ways to spend them.

* Tell them everything you know. -> n3_told
* Tell them it will be fine. -> n3_softened
* Say nothing. Keep the shift. -> n3_kept

== n3_told ==
~ told_truth true
~ listened +1
You tell them. All of it, including the part about the woman not writing down any names.
Monty says nothing, which is his way of thanking you. Chica cries in the way machines do,
which is quietly and in the wrong order. Freddy listens with his head tipped.
-> n3_dawn

== n3_softened ==
~ softened true
You tell them it will probably be fine. You use the word probably because it is load-bearing.
Roxanne thanks you. Chica believes you immediately, which is the worst outcome.
-> n3_dawn

== n3_kept ==
~ kept_quiet true
You do the rounds. You check the doors. You do not go back down the hall.
The notice stays on the wall and the building stays exactly as quiet as you left it.
-> n3_dawn

== n3_dawn ==
bg office_night
music none
Six o'clock. The paper is still taped at all four corners.
-> n3_dawn_out

== n3_dawn_out ==
if told_truth -> n3_dawn_told
if softened -> n3_dawn_soft
-> n3_dawn_silent

== n3_dawn_told ==
You spent your shift on something that will not go on any record.
It is the first honest hour this building has had in eleven years.
~ nights +1
-> n4_start

== n3_dawn_soft ==
You were kind, and kindness was the wrong tool, and you know it.
~ nights +1
-> n4_start

== n3_dawn_silent ==
You did the rounds. You checked the doors.
Somewhere behind you Chica is cleaning something that is already clean.
-> n4_start

# ============================================================
# NIGHT FOUR - the song
# ============================================================

== n4_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
Fourth night. The fan is not running.
You notice it the way you notice a stopped clock, which is immediately and all at once.
-> n4_dark

== n4_dark ==
music none
sfx power_down
The lights go out from the far end of the building inward, like something being folded.
No hum. No fan. No emergency lighting, because this building has never needed any.
Just dark, and then, from somewhere to your left, a music box.
-> n4_song

== n4_song ==
bg hall_corner
music music_box
show freddy idle at left
The song is small and mechanical and slightly out of tune with itself.
Freddy is standing in the doorway. He is not rushing anywhere and he is not smiling.
freddy: Do not get up.
freddy: I am not here to do the thing you think I am here to do.

* "What is that song?" -> n4_whatsong
* "I am not afraid of you." -> n4_notafraid

== n4_whatsong ==
~ knows_the_song true
~ listened +1
freddy: It is the only music nobody chose.
freddy: They bought a building and a box that plays this, and they put both of them here
and went home. The box is older than all of us.
freddy (wry): Sometimes I think I am just the box getting louder.
-> n4_reason

== n4_notafraid ==
~ aff_freddy +2
freddy: I know.
freddy (warm): That is why I am talking to you instead of standing here until the song stops.
freddy: I have done that to four people. It is not a conversation. I would like a conversation.
-> n4_reason

== n4_reason ==
freddy: Here is the thing I have never been able to ask anybody who works here.
freddy: When you leave at six, do you think about us at all.

* "Yes." -> n4_yes
* "No." -> n4_no
* "I do not know." -> n4_unknown

== n4_yes ==
~ aff_freddy +1
freddy: Hm.
freddy (wry): Everybody says yes. I have stopped believing it and I still ask.
-> n4_real

== n4_no ==
~ aff_freddy -2
freddy: Thank you.
freddy (idle): That is the first true thing anybody has said to me in here.
-> n4_real

== n4_unknown ==
~ aff_freddy +3
~ said_unknown true
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): Good.
freddy: That is the only answer I believe. It took eleven years and it was worth it.
-> n4_real

== n4_real ==
music none
The music box stops.
The silence afterwards is the loudest thing that has happened all week.
freddy: There. That is what I am.
freddy: The song plays, and then it stops, and I am standing in the doorway when it stops.
That is the whole of me. Nobody wrote me a part after this.

* "You are more than that." -> n4_more
* "That is not nothing." -> n4_notnothing
* "Does it have to be the whole of you?" -> n4_whole

== n4_more ==
~ aff_freddy +2
~ said_yes true
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): You are the only person who has ever said that in this building,
and you said it in the dark, to a thing with no part left.
-> n4_end

== n4_notnothing ==
~ aff_freddy +1
freddy: No. It is not nothing.
freddy (idle): It is a very small thing and I have had a long time to look at it.
-> n4_end

== n4_whole ==
~ aff_freddy +3
~ said_yes true
~ listened +1
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): No. I suppose it does not.
freddy: I have never thought of it as a question. I have only ever thought of it as an ending.
-> n4_end

== n4_end ==
bg office_night
music none
hide freddy
sfx power_up
The lights come back the same way they went, from the far end inward.
The fan starts. It sounds like nothing at all now.
-> n4_dawn

== n4_dawn ==
if said_unknown or said_yes -> n4_dawn_honest
-> n4_dawn_plain

== n4_dawn_honest ==
You sat in the dark and had a conversation with something that has never been
given a reason to expect one. It is not on the record. Neither is anything else here.
~ nights +1
-> n5_start

== n4_dawn_plain ==
You survived the fourth night by doing what you have always done, which is the rounds.
~ nights +1
-> n5_start
# ============================================================
# NIGHT FIVE - overtime
# ============================================================

== n5_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
Fifth night. The notice now has a date on it. It has been there since Tuesday
and you have been walking past it since Tuesday, which is what people do.
if nights >= 4 -> n5_start_known
-> n5_circuit

== n5_start_known ==
You have done every night of this week. Four of them went the way you meant them to
and one of them did not, and you know which one, and so does the building.
-> n5_circuit

== n5_circuit ==
The building is quieter tonight in the way a room is quiet when everyone in it
has already decided something and nobody has said it yet.
if let_quiet_stand -> n5_circuit_quiet
-> n5_route

== n5_circuit_quiet ==
You have spent this week saying almost nothing, deliberately, in the places
where saying something would have been easier.
Every one of them noticed. It turns out that was a way of being trusted,
which is not how you expected it to work.
-> n5_route

== n5_route ==
if told_truth and listened >= 4 -> n5_warm_circuit
if kept_quiet or softened -> n5_cold_circuit
-> n5_mid_circuit

# ---------- the warm circuit: they are waiting for you ----------

== n5_warm_circuit ==
bg dining
music none
show monty neutral at left
monty: You told us on Thursday.
monty: Nobody in eleven years has done that. I want you to understand the size of it.
monty (quiet): It is the only thing anybody has ever given me that I did not have to perform for.
hide monty
-> n5_chica_warm

== n5_chica_warm ==
bg east_corner
show chica neutral at center
chica: I know about the date.
chica (bright): I have decided to be very cheerful about it. It is going well.
chica (small): ...It is not going well.
chica: You said my name. On the first night you said my name and you have said it
every night since and I have been counting.
hide chica
-> n5_roxy_warm

== n5_roxy_warm ==
bg west_hall
show roxanne warm at center
if knows_roxanne -> n5_roxy_confess
roxanne: I have been trying to work out what to say to you all week.
roxanne (warm): I have not managed it. That is the whole speech.
hide roxanne
-> n5_freddy_final

== n5_roxy_confess ==
roxanne: I am going to say a true sentence and then I am going to go back to being me.
roxanne (warm): I was not performing for you. That has not happened before.
roxanne: Now get out of my hall.
hide roxanne
-> n5_freddy_final

== n5_mid_circuit ==
bg west_hall
music none
show roxanne flat at center
roxanne: Still here.
roxanne: Most people stop coming about now. There is nothing wrong with that.
roxanne: It is just a fact about people.
hide roxanne
-> n5_freddy_final

== n5_cold_circuit ==
bg west_hall
music none
The hall is empty. It usually is at this hour, and tonight that means something.
show roxanne cold at center
roxanne: I heard you on Thursday. Through the wall.
roxanne (cold): I am not angry. I am just adjusting.
hide roxanne
-> n5_freddy_final

# ---------- Freddy, last ----------

== n5_freddy_final ==
bg cove_open
music music_box
show freddy idle at right
freddy: You know what tonight is.
if knows_the_song -> n5_freddy_song
-> n5_freddy_asks

== n5_freddy_song ==
freddy (wry): You asked me about the song. In the dark, standing in a doorway,
while it was playing. I have not stopped thinking about that.
freddy: Nobody has ever asked me what it was. They have only ever asked me to stop.
-> n5_freddy_asks

== n5_freddy_asks ==
freddy: Do not say you do not. You have been very good about the notice.
freddy (wry): It has been the only performance in this building all week and I have enjoyed it.

* "What happens to you." -> n5_happens
* "I do not want to leave." -> n5_notleave

== n5_happens ==
freddy: Nobody knows. That is not a dodge, it is the actual answer.
freddy: There is a version where we are stored and a version where we are sold
and a version where we are simply not mentioned again.
freddy (idle): The last one is the one I think about.
-> n5_offer

== n5_notleave ==
~ aff_freddy +1
freddy: You have to leave. That is not a rule I made.
freddy (warm): The question is not whether you leave. It is what you take.
-> n5_offer

== n5_offer ==
freddy: So. One more time, and then I will let you do the last hour in peace.
freddy: Will you come back.

* "Yes. I will come back." -> n5_promise
* "No. I am not coming back." -> n5_refuse
* "I will stay past six tonight." -> n5_stay
* Say nothing. -> n5_silence

== n5_promise ==
~ promised true
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): All right.
freddy: I am going to write that in the ledger, which means nothing,
and I am going to think about it for a very long time, which means something.
hide freddy
-> n5_final

== n5_refuse ==
~ refused true
freddy: Thank you for saying it plainly.
freddy (idle): I would rather have a true no than a polite maybe. I have had a lot of polite maybes.
hide freddy
-> n5_final

== n5_stay ==
~ stayed true
freddy: ...
freddy: That is not how the building works.
freddy (warm): But it is how you work, and I have noticed, and I will remember it.
hide freddy
-> n5_final

== n5_silence ==
~ stayed false
freddy: Hm.
freddy (idle): I did not expect an answer. I asked because the asking is the thing.
hide freddy
-> n5_final

# ---------- dawn, and after ----------

== n5_final ==
bg office_night
music none
The last hour takes a long time and no time at all.
At six the lights come up, and the notice is still on the wall, with a date on it.
-> n5_endings

== n5_endings ==
if stayed -> ending_overtime
if promised and listened >= 5 and aff_freddy >= 5 -> ending_remembered
if promised -> ending_promised
if refused and (aff_monty >= 4 or aff_roxy >= 4 or aff_chica >= 4) -> ending_honest
if kept_quiet or softened -> ending_complicit
-> ending_gone

== ending_overtime ==
You do not clock out.
You sit in the chair that belonged to somebody whose name you never wrote down,
and the building gets quiet in the particular way it gets quiet when the staff have gone,
and you stay.
At seven somebody arrives and does not see you. At eight the lights go off again
from the far end inward and there is a music box and it is the only music nobody chose.
You are on overtime. Nobody is paying for it. You are not doing it for anybody.
Somewhere down the hall Chica is cleaning something that is already clean,
and she knows you are still here, and that is the first time in eleven years
that anybody in this building has not been alone at the end of a shift.
-> END

== ending_remembered ==
You clock out at six and you do come back, on the Tuesday, which is the day after the date.
The building is shut. The chairs are stacked the way chairs get stacked when nobody asks.
if asked_about_her -> ending_remembered_her
-> ending_remembered_close

== ending_remembered_her ==
You asked about her on the first night. Nobody had done that either.
You never got her name from a file or a rota -- you got it from Roxanne,
in a hallway, because you asked a real question and she decided you could hold it.
-> ending_remembered_close

== ending_remembered_close ==
You know all four names. You know which one performs, which one cleans,
which one counts eleven years in the dark, and which one stands in the doorway
when the song stops.
You write it down. All of it. Not for anybody, and not for a record,
because there is no record that would take it.
On the wall by the door, where the marker bruise is, you put her name back.
Some things get kept by exactly one person, and that is still kept.
-> END

== ending_promised ==
You clock out at six and you mean it when you say you will come back.
You do, for a while. Then the weeks get longer and the building stays shut
and coming back turns into remembering to come back, which is a different thing.
Freddy wrote it in a ledger he cannot show anybody.
It is the only copy, and it is accurate, and it is enough for one of you.
-> END

== ending_honest ==
You clock out at six and you say goodbye properly, which nobody has done here before.
You told the truth on Thursday and you told the truth tonight and both times
you said it in a building that has no way to keep it.
Whatever happens to this place, it happened to people who had been seen exactly once.
That is not rescue. It is not nothing either.
-> END

== ending_complicit ==
You clock out at six and you do not look at the notice on the way past.
On Thursday you chose the sentence that was easier to say and tonight you
chose the door that was nearer, and both times there was a reason,
and both reasons were good, and that is how it goes.
The building closes. Nobody writes any of it down.
Four people were in here for eleven years and the only thing anybody kept
was a piece of paper taped at all four corners, thanking them for their understanding.
-> END

== ending_gone ==
You clock out at six and you go home and you do not come back.
There is nothing wrong with that. It was a job.
You will think about it occasionally, in the way you think about a shift,
and the thinking will get smaller, and eventually it will be a thing that happened
in a building that is no longer there.
Four people waited eleven years for somebody to ask them a question.
You asked. Then you left. Both of those are true and only one of them lasted.
-> END
